# Replay

Import HostFiles from "./host_files.lg".
Import ChatRequest from "./chat_request.lg".
Import ChatReply from "./chat_reply.lg".

The replay provider: model answers read from recordings instead of bought. A
recording is keyed by the prompt hash over the exact request body, so it answers
exactly one question — this model, these messages, this temperature and token
allowance — and a changed question finds no recording rather than an old answer.
A directory holds `<hash>.json`, the reply in OpenRouter's own shape (read by the
same `parseChatReply` a live one is, cost and all), and `<hash>.request.json`,
the request it answers. A prompt without a recording leaves its request behind
and stops with its hash, so the answer can be recorded and the run repeated.

## To replayReplyPath (dir: Text, sha: Text) -> Text:
    Return dir + "/" + sha + ".json".

## To replayRequestPath (dir: Text, sha: Text) -> Text:
    Return dir + "/" + sha + ".request.json".

## Note
A reply in OpenRouter's shape, for authoring a recording: the answer as the first
choice's message, its token counts and its cost in micro-dollars.

## To replyDocument (id: Text, model: Text, content: Text, promptTokens: Int, completionTokens: Int, costMicros: Int) -> Text:
    Let message be a new JObj with entries [a new JEntry with key "role" and val (a new JStr with s "assistant"), a new JEntry with key "content" and val (a new JStr with s content)].
    Let choice be a new JObj with entries [a new JEntry with key "finish_reason" and val (a new JStr with s "stop"), a new JEntry with key "message" and val message].
    Let mutable cost be "0".
    If costMicros is greater than 0:
        Set cost to jsonRenderDec(costMicros, 0 - 6).
    Let counts be "\"prompt_tokens\":{promptTokens},\"completion_tokens\":{completionTokens},\"cost\":" + cost.
    Let head be "{{\"id\":" + jsonQuote(id) + ",\"model\":" + jsonQuote(model) + ",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"choices\":[" + jsonSerialize(choice) + "]".
    Return head + ",\"usage\":{{" + counts + "}}}}".

## Note
The recorded answer to `request`, or the stop naming the missing recording after
writing down the request it would answer.

## To replayComplete (dir: Text, request: ChatRequest) -> Result of ChatReply and Text:
    Let sha be promptSha(request).
    Let path be replayReplyPath(dir, sha).
    If pathExists(path):
        Inspect readText(path):
            When Err (e):
                Return a new Err with error "the recording {path} is unreadable: " + e.
            When Ok (text):
                Inspect parseChatReply(text):
                    When Err (e):
                        Return a new Err with error "the recording {path} is not a reply: " + e.
                    When Ok (reply):
                        Return a new Ok with value reply.
    Let made be ensureDir(dir).
    Let written be writeText(replayRequestPath(dir, sha), chatRequestJson(request)).
    Return a new Err with error "no recorded reply for prompt {sha}; its request is at " + replayRequestPath(dir, sha).

## Note
A recording made: the reply to `request` under its prompt hash, the request
beside it. Answers the hash.

## To recordReply (dir: Text, request: ChatRequest, replyText: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Let sha be promptSha(request).
    Let made be ensureDir(dir).
    Let wrote be writeText(replayRequestPath(dir, sha), chatRequestJson(request)).
    Inspect writeText(replayReplyPath(dir, sha), replyText):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (done):
            Return a new Ok with value sha.
    Return a new Err with error "unrecorded".
